    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java` (mirrors the existing `TelephoneE164` pattern): `normalize()` trims, collapses whitespace runs to a single space, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Expansion is token-based so an abbreviation embedded in a longer word (e.g. `STANMORE`) is untouched. Null/blank input yields `\"\"`.\n\n**`ValidateOwner`** \u2014 normalizes the address *before* the required-field check and writes the normalized value back onto the request. Because it publishes the request for later steps, the normalized address flows through `BuildOwner` \u2192 the entity \u2192 the response, so it's stored and returned. A value that is blank only after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) now yields `400`.\n\n**`CheckHouseholdUnique`** and **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 address comparisons (duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` derivation/stamping) now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` for both the new request and every existing owner, so all address comparisons use the normalized form.\n\nThe three acceptance tests cover the three behaviours (whitespace/case collapse, abbreviation expansion, and blank-after-normalize rejection) and all pass.",
